    "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/program-administrative-coordinator/": {
      "title": "Program Administrative Coordinator",
      "description": "Program Administrative Coordinator - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / Program Administrative Coordinator Program Administrative Coordinator Posted September 2, 2026 Doctor of Nurse Anesthesia Practice (DNAP) Program Bert Bradford School of Health Sciences, University of Charleston Position Summary: The DNAP Program Administrative Coordinator provides comprehensive administrative and operational support for the Doctor of Nurse Anesthesia Practice (DNAP) Program. This position works closely with the Program Director, Assistant Program Director/Clinical Director, faculty, students, university departments, clinical affiliates, and other stakeholders to support the effective operation of the program. The Coordinator plays an essential role in maintaining program organization, student and faculty records, accreditation documentation, clinical and academic scheduling, communication, meetings, and program events. The position requires a high degree of organization, professionalism, confidentiality, attention to detail, and the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines within a complex graduate healthcare education environment. The DNAP Program Administrative Coordinator reports directly to the DNAP Program Director and works collaboratively with the Assistant Program Director/Clinical Director, DNAP faculty, university administration, clinical partners, and other individuals involved in the administration and delivery of the program. Essential Responsibilities: The DNAP Program Administrative Coordinator is expected to maintain a working knowledge of program policies, procedures, academic calendars, accreditation requirements, and administrative processes necessary to support the effective operation of the DNAP Program. The Coordinator serves as an important organizational resource for the program and contributes to maintaining accurate documentation, effective communication, regulatory readiness, and a professional environment for students, faculty, and program stakeholders. Provide administrative support to the Program Director, Assistant Program Director/Clinical Director, and DNAP faculty. ·        Coordinate daily administrative operations of the DNAP Program. ·        Maintain program calendars, schedules, deadlines, files, and administrative records. ·        Prepare correspondence, reports, agendas, meeting materials, presentations, and other program documents. ·        Coordinate meetings and maintain meeting schedules for program committees, faculty, students, and other stakeholders. ·        Record, prepare, distribute, and maintain official meeting minutes as assigned. ·        Assist with purchasing, invoices, reimbursements, memberships, travel arrangements, and other program-related financial processes. ·        Maintain office supplies, educational materials, and other program resources. ·        Serve as a primary administrative point of contact for students, applicants, faculty, clinical partners, and university departments. ·        Maintain accurate student records and assist with tracking required academic, clinical, and program documentation. ·        Assist with student onboarding, orientation, registration, graduation, and other progression-related activities. ·        Monitor completion and submission of required student documentation and notify appropriate program leadership of missing or incomplete requirements. ·        Assist with scheduling classes, examinations, meetings, advising sessions, and other academic activities. ·        Support administration and coordination of program examinations and standardized testing activities, including the SEE and NCE preparation processes as directed. ·        Assist with maintaining student rosters, contact information, academic records, and program progression documentation. ·        Coordinate student communications regarding deadlines, schedules, program activities, and administrative requirements. ·        Maintain confidentiality of student educational records in accordance with FERPA, institutional policy, and applicable regulations. ·        Provide administrative support for clinical scheduling and clinical education activities. ·        Maintain current records related to clinical sites, student assignments, clinical rotations, and required documentation. ·        Assist with communication among students, faculty, clinical coordinators, clinical sites, and affiliated organizations. ·        Track required clinical documentation, evaluations, specialty rotations, certifications, and other program requirements as assigned. ·        Assist with maintaining clinical affiliation information and documentation. ·        Support coordination of student clinical onboarding requirements for affiliated clinical sites. ·        Assist the Program Director and faculty with maintaining documentation necessary for continued compliance with the Council on Accreditation of Nurse Anesthesia Educational Programs (COA) standards and institutional requirements. ·        Maintain organized electronic and/or physical accreditation files and supporting evidence. ·        Assist with preparation and organization of documentation for annual reports, self-study reports, accreditation reviews, site visits, and other regulatory or institutional reporting requirements. ·        Track recurring accreditation, program evaluation, and reporting deadlines. ·        Assist with maintaining documentation related to program policies, procedures, outcomes, evaluations, committee activities, faculty qualifications, and student progression. ·        Support collection and organization of data used for program evaluation and continuous quality improvement. ·        Maintain current versions of program policies, handbooks, forms, organizational documents, and other official program materials. ·        Provide administrative support for faculty meetings, advisory committees, evaluation activities, and other program committees. ·        Coordinate meeting schedules, agendas, supporting documents, attendance records, and minutes. ·        Maintain faculty files and assist with tracking required licenses, certifications, professional development, evaluations, and other documentation as assigned. ·        Assist with faculty onboarding and administrative processes for new faculty, adjunct faculty, guest lecturers, and clinical educators. ·        Support faculty with classroom scheduling, educational materials, examinations, student communication, and program events. ·        Provide administrative support for the DNAP admissions process. ·        Respond to general inquiries from prospective applicants and direct program-specific questions to appropriate faculty or leadership. ·        Assist with open houses, recruitment activities, interviews, applicant communication, and admissions events. ·        Coordinate interview schedules and prepare applicant materials for faculty review. ·        Maintain appropriate admissions documentation and records in accordance with institutional policies. ·        Assist with communication and onboarding of accepted students. ·        Assist with planning and coordination of orientation, graduation, open houses, student presentations, professional development activities, and other program events. ·        Coordinate meeting spaces, technology, catering, materials, attendance, and other event logistics as needed. ·        Assist with student and faculty participation in professional meetings and program-sponsored activities. ·        Support dissemination of program announcements, recognition activities, and other communications. ·        Maintain organized electronic program files and shared drives. ·        Utilize university and healthcare-system information systems as required for program operations. ·        Maintain spreadsheets, databases, tracking systems, and reports used to monitor program requirements and outcomes. ·        Assist with learning management systems, student information systems, scheduling platforms, survey/evaluation systems, and other educational technology. ·        Ensure program documentation is appropriately organized, accessible, secure, and retained according to applicable policies. ·        Communicate professionally and effectively with students, faculty, administrators, clinical partners, applicants, and members of the public. ·        Handle confidential and sensitive information with discretion. ·        Demonstrate professionalism, dependability, initiative, and responsiveness. ·        Establish effective working relationships across multiple departments and organizations. ·        Exercise sound judgment in determining when issues should be referred to the Program Director or other program leadership. ·        Other duties may be assigned as necessary to support the mission, accreditation, and effective operation of the DNAP Program. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Associate degree or equivalent combination of education and relevant administrative experience. Demonstrated experience providing administrative or program coordination support. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, including Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook, and Teams. Strong organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Ability to manage multiple responsibilities, deadlines, and competing priorities. Strong attention to detail and accuracy. Ability to maintain confidentiality and appropriately handle sensitive student and personnel information. Exceptional organizational and time-management skills. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to work independently while functioning effectively as part of a collaborative team. Ability to anticipate program needs and proactively address administrative responsibilities. Ability to prioritize tasks in a fast-paced academic and clinical environment. High level of accuracy and attention to detail. Strong problem-solving skills and professional judgment. Ability to interact effectively with graduate students, faculty, healthcare professionals, administrators, and external stakeholders. Commitment to supporting the mission, goals, and continuous improvement of the DNAP Program. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree. Previous experience in higher education, graduate education, healthcare, or an academic healthcare environment. Experience supporting nursing, nurse anesthesia, medical, or other health professions education programs. Familiarity with accreditation and regulatory documentation. Experience with student information systems, learning management systems, clinical tracking systems, and electronic document management. Experience coordinating meetings, committees, events, and complex schedules. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit cover letter, resume, references, and salary requirements to: Megan Orphanos – meganorphanos@ucwv.edu Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future visa sponsorship. The University is unable to sponsor visas or green cards at this time. The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift © 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"
    },
    "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/assistant-director-of-admissions/": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Admissions",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Admissions - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / Assistant Director of Admissions Assistant Director of Admissions Posted August 25, 2026 Assistant Director of Admissions Admissions, University of Charleston Position Summary: The Assistant Director of Admissions serves as the primary application reviewer and processor for all domestic Charleston 4-year Undergraduate, 2-year Associate, and Graduate Health Science programs. Under the direct supervision of the Director of Admissions Operations, the Assistant Director of Admissions will execute daily application management, cyclical enrolled student file audits, transcript management, and run application imports in addition to all other vendor imports to provide comprehensive data management support for the Office of Admissions. Additionally, this position will be responsible for supervision of Graduate Assistants, as well as planning and coordinating on campus recruitment events and Admissions Counselor travel. Essential Responsibilities: Provision and review all incoming Undergraduate applications for Charleston 4 year programs (and Charleston ADN) as well as provision all Graduate Health Science applications for programmatic review in CRM Recruit, aiming for a 1-2 business day turnaround for all completed application packets. Maintain a daily schedule of application imports from various vendors, such as Common App and Universal App. Oversee manual hardcopy application entry into CRM Recruit to ensure all are entered and reviewed within 1-2 business days. Maintain a daily schedule of Inquiry and Suspect imports from various vendors such as ENCOURA, Niche, Sage Scholars, etc. Maintain a daily schedule of retrieving transcripts from various vendors such as Parchment, National Student Clearinghouse, SCOIR, etc. Conduct routine enrolled student file audits leading up to each semester’s census period (“Freeze Day”) to ensure data accuracy and alignment. Provide weekly reports regarding Applicant > Admit yield. Coordinate with various campus stakeholders regarding students seeking readmission to the University. Maintain a daily schedule of coding Enrollment Deposits received in both CRM Recruit & Colleague to ensure consistent email credential generation. Assist with various operational projects such as Fall application configuration rollouts, Common App configurations, and CRM template updates. Plan and execute on-campus recruitment events. Coordinate Admissions Counselor travel to off-campus recruitment events. Coordinate execution of “Home to UC” recruitment program. Supervise departmental Graduate Assistants. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications: Earned bachelor’s degree, master’s degree preferred A minimum of 2 years professional experience, preferably in an education or enrollment management setting Strong written and verbal communication skills Collaborative mindset Ability to build and manage a consistent processing schedule Ability to work independently Familiarity with customer relationship software (CRM) system Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit cover letter, current resume, names of three professional references, and salary requirements to: Jason Sammons, jasonsammons@ucwv.edu Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future visa sponsorship.  The University is unable to sponsor visas or green cards at this time. The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift © 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"
    },
    "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/international-enrollment-coordinator/": {
      "title": "International Enrollment Coordinator",
      "description": "International Enrollment Coordinator - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Charleston / International Enrollment Coordinator International Enrollment Coordinator Posted August 25, 2026 International Enrollment Coordinator Office of Admissions, University of Charleston Position Summary: Under the direct supervision of the Director of Admissions, the International Enrollment Coordinator has the responsibility for implementing multi-channel marketing and recruitment strategies related to international student enrollment. The International Enrollment Coordinator will be responsible for meeting territory and programmatic enrollment goals through the execution of various approaches, including but not limited to participation in in-person and virtual recruitment events (both on and off campus), and extensive communication with various constituents. Application management and decision making are an integral part of the position. Some nights and weekends are required. Essential Responsibilities: Be knowledgeable about the University of Charleston’s programs, features, facilities, scholarships, and financial aid opportunities. Be able to articulate same in a professional, consistent manner Work with supervisor to understand territorial and programmatic recruitment goals and utilize multi- channel communication strategies to achieve these goals. Evaluate the effectiveness of various approaches utilized Hit enrollment targets weekly, monthly, and annually Manage international application review and associated decision making in a timely manner (typically 1 – 3 business days) in accordance with the goals of the Office of Admissions Interface with University personnel (i.e.: faculty, coaches, deans, support, and administrative staff) regularly Review scholarship eligibility and awards with prospective students Demonstrate strong customer service orientation Be proficient in the use of the University’s management information systems (Recruit and Colleague) and Microsoft Office applications Provide support to broader Admissions Office application and data processing needs Carry out special projects and other duties as assigned Qualifications: This is an entry-level position that requires a Bachelor’s degree Experience in sales, marketing, and/or higher education is preferred Candidate must be a goal-oriented self-starter who can handle multiple projects in a fast-paced environment Candidate must have a reliable car and a valid driver’s license Must be able to lift and carry marketing/promotional materials (up to 30 pounds) Must have excellent written and oral communication skills, strong computer, and organizational skills Be able to think, plan, and execute strategically Candidate must have a customer service orientation and utilize relationship building techniques Additionally, the successful candidate will be a team player who demonstrates flexibility and the willingness to “pitch in” when needed The job will require occasional weekends and holidays Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit cover letter, resume, references, and salary requirements to: Jason Sammons, jasonsammons@ucwv.edu Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future visa sponsorship.  The University is unable to sponsor visas or green cards at this time. The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift © 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"
    },
    "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/dean/": {
      "title": "Dean",
      "description": "Dean - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Charleston / Dean Dean Posted August 20, 2026 Dean School of Business, University of Charleston Position Summary: The Dean of the School of Business is the chief academic and administrative officer of the School and a member of the University Leadership Team. The position requires an energetic and highly collaborative faculty colleague with a demonstrated commitment to student success, teaching excellence, transformative leadership, and community engagement. This is an on-campus, 12-month administrative appointment with faculty rank, reporting directly to the Provost. Essential Responsibilities: Promoting the University’s values of student focus, quality, and integrity, and its mission to educate each student for a life of productive work, enlightened living, and community involvement Collaborating with University leadership to support institutional and school goals relating to academic excellence, student achievement, enrollment growth, and financial stability Systematically monitoring and assessing the School’s strengths, weaknesses, threats, and opportunities in consultation with faculty, staff, and institutional leadership Continuously monitoring student demand and university contribution for each School of Business academic program Leading planning processes to enhance the academic programs, brand identity and market appeal of the School and the University as a student-centered, teaching-focused institution Partnering with University leadership to support School and institutional admissions, marketing, enrollment, retention, graduation, and revenue goals Promoting a culture of innovation, transparency, and shared governance in the School and across the University by encouraging the open, honest, and respectful discussion of issues Ensuring effective communication with internal and external stakeholders in support of School and institutional goals Collaborating with School and institutional leaders to support University academic, athletic, and extra-curricular activities, including interdisciplinary initiatives Increasing graduate and undergraduate enrollment through new student recruitment and returning student retention Growing in-seat and online programs that meet the needs of learners of all ages Collaborating with the School of Leadership which serves adult learners through distance learning leadership and cybersecurity programs Supervising the assessment of academic programs, student learning outcomes, student support services, and administrative functions in the School Facilitating the preparation of School and program information in support of University publications, catalogs, and recruitment materials, including the University website Leading the preparation and administration of budgets for academic programs and administrative functions in the School, aligning budget requests with University goals and priorities Maintaining ACBSP accreditation Practicing data-informed and evidence-based decision making in collaboration with School faculty Recommending faculty and staff appointments, including department chairs and program directors, in consultation with the Provost and, as appropriate, University leadership Supervising faculty and staff personnel issues, including hiring academically/professional qualified faculty, contract renewals, promotions, and disciplinary decisions Monitoring and assessing faculty and staff performance, including department chairs and program directors, on the basis of the University’s personnel policies and practices Identifying and supporting professional development opportunities for faculty and staff, including the promotion of faculty scholarship consistent with University policy Ensuring an equitable workload for staff and faculty, consistent with University practices Advancing the reputation of the School by building community relationships and initiating outreach efforts, including active engagement of alumni, advisory boards, and other professional networks Pursuing external funding opportunities and grant initiatives to promote School and institutional goals in consultation with faculty and institutional leadership Ensuring School compliance with regulatory requirements set by accrediting and governmental bodies at state, federal, and professional association levels Other duties as assigned Qualifications: A terminal degree in a business-related discipline or significant professional experience in a business-related field A minimum of 10 years’ experience as a faculty colleague and a record of progressively responsible administrative appointments in higher education or related fields Documented success in promoting innovation in business education and student success initiatives, including proven recruitment and retention strategies Familiarity with ACBSP or other business school accreditation standards Evidence of strong leadership, interpersonal, communication, and budget management skills. Accomplishments in the areas of teaching, research, and service that would merit appointment at the rank of associate professor or professor Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit a current CV, contact information for five professional references, and a cover letter addressing the criteria and qualifications cited above to: Shationya Ralph – sobusiness@ucwv.edu Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future visa sponsorship.  The University is unable to sponsor visas or green cards at this time. The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift © 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"
    },
    "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/assistant-or-associate-professor-of-accounting/": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Charleston / Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting Posted August 20, 2026 Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting School of Business, University of Charleston Position Summary: This faculty member will teach undergraduate accounting courses and contribute to the continued growth of the Accounting program. There is potential for program director responsibilities —including leadership in curriculum development, assessment, and community engagement—for qualified candidates. The University is teaching‑focused and student‑centered. The School of Business serves over 300 business students with undergraduate majors in Accounting, Business Analytics, Digital Marketing, Entrepreneurship, Financial Planning, Management, Marketing, Professional Selling, Sport Business, Sport Analytics, and Sport Media. Our students come from diverse backgrounds and are primarily full‑time and residential. The School is accredited by the Accreditation Council for Business Schools & Programs (ACBSP). The position reports to the Dean of the School of Business. Essential Responsibilities: Teaching primarily in‑seat financial accounting courses, including Intermediate Accounting, Advanced Accounting, and Auditing. Hybrid or online courses may be part of the teaching load as needed. Contributing to program and course design, development, and assessment; mentoring students through organizations and activities; and engaging with community professionals. Academic advising of students. Scholarly activity consistent with expectations for faculty at an ACBSP‑accredited school. University service through committee membership and participation in shared governance. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications: Master’s degree in accounting or related field preferred. Candidates with a bachelor’s degree and significant professional experience (e.g., CPA) will be considered, with the expectation of completing a master’s degree within an agreed‑upon timeframe. CPA credential or substantial professional experience as a financial accountant or auditor. Energy, enthusiasm, and excellence in teaching; experience teaching in multiple modalities (in‑seat, hybrid, online) preferred. Record of applied scholarship or professional contributions. Experience using appropriate technology in course development and delivery. Ability to engage students in professional and career preparation. Willingness to actively participate in service to the university, school, and community. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit cover letter, current resume, names of three professional references, and salary requirements to: Shationya Ralph: shationyaralph@ucwv.edu Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future visa sponsorship.  The University is unable to sponsor visas or green cards at this time. The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift © 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"
    },
    "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/lab-assistant/": {
      "title": "Lab Assistant",
      "description": "Lab Assistant - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Charleston / Lab Assistant Lab Assistant Posted August 20, 2026 Lab Assistant Master of Science in Occupational Therapy, Bert Bradford School of Health Sciences, University of Charleston Position Summary: This position serves as the Master of Science in Occupational Therapy (MSOT) Lab Assistant to the MSOT Program Director, Academic Fieldwork Coordinator, and all MSOT Faculty, both on-site and remote, for the Bert Bradford School of Health Sciences and performs all duties related thereto. The Occupational Therapy Lab Assistant supports the organization, delivery, and maintenance of lab-based learning experiences aligned with the Accreditation Council for Occupational Therapy Education (ACOTE) Standards for occupational therapy education. This position plays a key role in facilitating student skill development, coordinating with faculty to implement and assess competencies, and ensuring the lab environment supports the program’s curricular goals. Responsibilities also include contributing to course tasks, program evaluation, assisting with events that support student recruitment and retention, and participating in broader university initiatives as requested. Essential Responsibilities: The candidate must have the minimum necessary knowledge, skills, and abilities expected for the position. Organize and maintain a simulated occupational therapy lab for student practice and skill acquisition Prepare classrooms and labs for scheduled instructional activities Assist students with accessing and using equipment and resources during lab sessions Monitor and support safe and secure use of lab space and equipment Track inventory and maintain equipment and supplies; assist with purchasing as needed Complete all equipment safety checks routinely Maintain clear communication with faculty regarding lab needs and operations Support course instructors with skill-based student learning, evaluation, and remediation Recommend additional resources (equipment, software) to enhance lab learning Participate in program-related events such as admissions activities, student orientations, open houses, and all MSOT student events Administer elements of the program’s assessment system related to lab and fieldwork preparation Mentor and support underperforming students through remediation efforts Complete pre and post lab disinfection procedures Assist with fieldwork processes as requested Travel Requirements: Travel to assist with fieldwork site visits, student community service events, and any other student related learning offsite events Physical Demands: This position requires occasional climbing, stooping, crawling, lifting, pulling, and pushing up to 50 lbs. Frequent walking, standing, and balancing is necessary The role demands constant sitting, hand/wrist movements, verbal communication, and near/far vision with depth and color perception Physical strength to exert 20–50 lbs. occasionally, 10–25 lbs. frequently, and up to 10 lbs. constantly is required Perform other professional duties as assigned Qualifications: Must be an occupational therapy assistant with a minimum of an associate’s degree. Holds and maintains a current occupational therapy license in West Virginia (or eligible). Minimum of three years of clinical experience. Strong interpersonal and communication skills and the ability to work collaboratively with faculty, students, staff, and external partners. Demonstrated organizational skills and attention to detail. Proficiency in computer and educational technologies. Commitment to student-centered support and professional integrity. Ability to work independently, demonstrate initiative, and assess operations to improve program effectiveness. Must maintain confidentiality and comply with institutional and accreditation policies. Accommodate a day, evening and weekend lab schedule for hybrid program. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit cover letter, current resume, names of three professional references, and salary requirements to: Nicole Scheiman – nicolescheiman@ucwv.edu Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future visa sponsorship.  The University is unable to sponsor visas or green cards at this time. The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift © 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"
    },
    "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/assistant-or-associate-professor-doctor-of-executive-leadership-program/": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor,  Doctor of Executive Leadership Program",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor, Doctor of Executive Leadership Program - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Charleston / Assistant or Associate Professor,  Doctor of Executive Leadership Program Assistant or Associate Professor,  Doctor of Executive Leadership Program Posted July 29, 2026 School of Leadership, University of Charleston Position Summary: This graduate faculty member will facilitate courses in the Doctor of Executive (DEL) program, participate in faculty governance, be active in program recruitment, engage in scholarship related to Leadership degree programs, and collaboratively support the mission, vision, and values of the program consistent with developmental, student-centered adult learning principles. Academic rank commensurate with experience. This position is contingent upon the availability of funding. Essential Responsibilities: Facilitate a full-time load in the DEL program Serve as academic advisor for students in the DEL program as appropriate Engage in scholarship in program specialty area and maintain currency and quality of curriculum related to that area Participate in department, school, and University faculty governance Contribute to departmental and program committees, including assessment, curriculum, social responsibility, mentoring, or intellectual community Mentor doctoral students as assigned Collaborate on DEL program and university developmental activities and intellectual community events Attend and participate in doctoral residency Actively participate in program recruitment Other duties as assigned Qualifications: Earned doctoral degree required; leadership-related discipline preferred Demonstrated knowledge of adult learning principles, online facilitation, outcomes-based learning, and assessment Experience in doctoral-level instruction and dissertation committee work Excellent organizational and communication skills, and willingness to work in a collaborative environment Experience in recruitment and building strategic relationships/partnerships Effective inter-departmental collaboration to support program value add and mission alignment Technological competence in word processing, virtual meeting platforms, presentation software, spreadsheets, student database systems (Ellucian preferred), learning management systems Event planning and grant writing experience desired The position requires access to sensitive and confidential student information. Applicant must be able to adhere to student confidentiality policies and procedures Evening and weekend work is required Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, current resume, names of three professional references, and salary requirements to: Dr. Kristen Dugan: kristendugan@ucwv.edu Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future visa sponsorship.  The University is unable to sponsor visas or green cards at this time. The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift © 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"
    },
    "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/administrative-assistant-part-time/": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant (Part-Time)",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant (Part-Time) - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Charleston / Administrative Assistant (Part-Time) Administrative Assistant (Part-Time) Posted June 18, 2026 Administrative Assistant (Part-Time) Provost Office, University of Charleston Position Summary: The Administrative Assistant to the Provost is a half-time (20 hours/week), 12-month administrative position reporting directly to the Provost. The staff member in this position works collaboratively with the Provost Office staff, the Executive Administrative Assistant to the President and Provost’s Offices, and other University offices. Essential Responsibilities: Prepare adjunct faculty contracts Gathering of information Mail merge Excel sheet and contract file Upload contracts for Dean and Provost signatures Upload contracts for adjunct faculty signature Create master adjunct faculty sheet Create adjunct SharePoint with Payroll Office/add relevant contracts and master sheet Assist Executive Administrative Assistant to President and Provost’s Offices with faculty overload contracts Course builds for University and Honors programs Assist Associate Provost with classroom assignments In-seat course classroom assignments Requests for day-to-day classroom usage from Athletics and extracurricular groups Provost List Mail merge Provost List letters based on list provided by Registrar Provost List certificates Assist Associate Provost with maintenance of Academic Integrity Violation records Collaborate with Executive Administrative Assistant on maintenance of Provost Office Dropbox Sign Assist Associate Provost with Academic Catalog Prepare payroll paperwork for Provost Office, University Program, and Academic Success Center staff (PEs, TAs, Tutors, etc.) Prepare Dual Role forms for faculty/staff teaching in University, Honors, Innovation and other programs as needed Other duties as assigned Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree preferred Two (2) years of administrative support or office management experience Proficient in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, Outlook, PowerPoint) Ability to work independently and in accordance with University policies and procedures Willingness to take the initiative to create/modify processes to promote productivity Excellent organizational and problem-solving skills, including attention to detail Good verbal and written communication skills Ability to maintain confidentiality at all times Commitment to great customer service Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit cover letter, resume, references, and salary requirements to: Provost Office provostoffice@ucwv.edu Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future visa sponsorship.  The University is unable to sponsor visas or green cards at this time The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift © 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"
    },
    "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/physics-adjunct-department-of-natural-sciences/": {
      "title": "Physics Adjunct – Department of Natural Sciences",
      "description": "Physics Adjunct - Department of Natural Sciences - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Charleston / Physics Adjunct – Department of Natural Sciences Physics Adjunct – Department of Natural Sciences Posted June 1, 2026 Physics Adjunct – Department of Natural Sciences School of Arts & Sciences, University of Charleston Position Summary: The Department of Natural Sciences at the University of Charleston, Charleston, WV, invites applications for a part-time adjunct position to teach Introductory Physics I and Introductory Physics II in support of undergraduate majors in Biology and related Health Science majors. Physics I (with lab) covers topics in mechanics, thermodynamics, and waves, including motion in one and two dimensions, forces, energy, momentum, collisions, rotational motion, properties of solids and fluids, thermal processes, vibrations, and sound. Physics II (with lab) focuses on electricity and magnetism, light and optics, relativity, and introductions to quantum, atomic, and nuclear physics. The Adjunct position is in-seat at the University of Charleston campus in Charleston, WV, beginning August 2026. Candidates must be available to teach in the classroom during the day on the Charleston campus. Physics I is fall semester and Physics II is spring semester. Essential Responsibilities: Primary duties include, but are not limited to Updating class syllabus Using LMS to report grades, post assignments, and communications Holding out-of-class conferences with students as required Presenting instruction based on the competencies and performance levels of the course Meeting all designated class periods Submitting quarterly assessments and final grades Posting feedback and grades to the LMS in a timely manner Maintaining communication with students and other faculty members Qualifications: Ph.D. in a related field or M.S. in the content area, and demonstrated teaching experience A commitment to undergraduate education with expertise in math, physics, or physical chemistry, and demonstrated dedication to STEM education Excellent communication skills, both verbal and written The screening of applications will begin immediately, and applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit a current vitae/resume, contact information for three professional references, and a cover letter addressing the criteria and qualifications identified to: School of Arts and Sciences – artsandsciences@ucwv.edu Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future visa sponsorship.  The University is unable to sponsor visas or green cards at this time. The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift © 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"
    },
    "https://www.ucwv.edu/job-postings/student-engagement-retention-coordinator/": {
      "title": "Student Engagement & Retention Coordinator",
      "description": "Student Engagement & Retention Coordinator - University of Charleston Skip to main content University of Charleston University of Charleston Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu Charleston, West Virginia Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply Open Search Close Search Open Menu Close Menu About UC Programs and Schools Admissions Alumni Athletics Explore Programs Financial Aid Giving Honors College Innovation at UC UC Life myUC Search search Top Searches Cost Financial Aid Catalog Events Military Bookstore Transcripts Schoenbaum Library Home / Job Postings / UC-Charleston / Student Engagement & Retention Coordinator Student Engagement & Retention Coordinator Posted March 30, 2026 Student Engagement & Retention Coordinator Title III University of Charleston Position Summary: The Title III Student Success Coordinator plays a critical role in supporting student persistence, engagement, and degree completion. This position provides individualized outreach, academic and personal support, and coordinates initiatives that strengthen retention and foster a vibrant, inclusive campus environment. The coordinator works collaboratively with faculty, advisors, and student support staff to identify student challenges, address barriers, and implement engagement opportunities that promote a culture of success for all students, including students with disabilities. The position is funded by a grant from the U.S. Department of Education and therefore contingent on the renewal of the award. Although the position is paid with federal funds, the individual will be governed by University of Charleston policies and procedures. Essential Responsibilities: Provide proactive advising and individualized support to students, focusing on academic progress, personal development, and overall persistence. Monitor student progress, conduct outreach, and connect students with appropriate campus and community resources. Identify and address academic, social, and personal barriers impacting student success. Coordinate, implement, and assess retention focused programs aligned with Title III project goals. Plan, promote, and execute campus-wide engagement initiatives that enhance student experience and strengthen student belonging. Support engagement and retention efforts for all students, including students with disabilities. Work collaboratively with faculty, advisors, student support services, and campus partners to maintain a coordinated and holistic approach to student success. Contribute to institutional retention strategies through cross departmental partnerships. Maintain accurate records of student interactions, outreach, and program participation. Assist with data collection, evaluation, and reporting related to retention and student success initiatives. Occasional travel to Beckley campus may be required. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in educational counseling, higher education, or a related field required; master’s degree preferred. Three to five years of professional experience in higher education, with emphasis on student success, retention, support services, or engagement. Strong interpersonal, communication, organizational, and problem-solving skills. Demonstrated ability to build effective relationships with diverse student populations and collaborate across departments. Commitment to fostering an inclusive and supportive campus environment. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit a current vitae/resume, contact information for three professional references, and a cover letter addressing the criteria and qualification identified to: Provost Office provostoffice@ucwv.edu The University of Charleston is an Equal Opportunity Employer Explore Programs Give Request Info Visit Apply 2300 MacCorkle Ave SE Charleston, WV 25304 1-800-995-4682 (GO UC) Contact Us Giving Visiting Campus Campus Safety and Security myUC Privacy Policy Consumer Information and Disclosures Campus Directory Employment News Events Bookstore Title IX Support UC Unlock a world of limitless opportunity for our students. Make a Gift © 2026 University of Charleston Instagram Twitter Facebook Youtube LinkedIn"
    },
